WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.300
Next, which realm.

2
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.900
Oracle Cloud is divided into realms.

3
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.750
The commercial realm, O C
1, is what the lab uses.

4
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:13.404
Oracle's US Government Cloud page lists
the Announcements service in realm O C 2,

5
00:00:13.404 --> 00:00:16.488
at two government regions,
Langley and Luke.

6
00:00:16.488 --> 00:00:21.321
For realm O C 3, Oracle's page wasn't
readable when the chapter was written,

7
00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:26.400
so its endpoint is not yet specified,
and the kit refuses it with that reason.

8
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.487
Why does it matter?

9
00:00:27.487 --> 00:00:31.438
A government tenancy read in the
commercial realm returns nothing.

10
00:00:31.438 --> 00:00:34.244
So the settings name the realm and region,

11
00:00:34.244 --> 00:00:37.100
and a region outside the realm is refused.
